title: Presidential Election campaigning
subtitle: It's campaign season.
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.hindenburg_funds = 0;
Q.hindenburg_support = 0;
if (Q.nsdap_candidate == "Hitler") {
    Q.workers_nsdap += 3;
    Q.new_middle_nsdap += 4;
    Q.old_middle_nsdap += 4;
    Q.catholics_nsdap += 2;
    Q.rural_nsdap += 4;
    Q.unemployed_nsdap += 4;
    Q.new_middle_dnvp -= 2;
    Q.old_middle_dnvp -= 2; 
    Q.unemployed_kpd -= 2;
} else if (Q.nsdap_candidate == "Göring") {
    Q.old_middle_nsdap += 4;
    Q.old_middle_dnvp -= 4;
    Q.rural_nsdap += 2;
    Q.rural_dnvp -= 2;
    Q.workers_kpd += 3;
    Q.workers_nsdap -= 3;
}
!}
tags: event
view-if: year = 1932 and month >= 2 and presidential_election_campaigning_seen = 1
face-image: img/dvp_campaign.jpg
max-visits: 1
go-to: candidate_selection


= Presidential Election campaigning

The NSDAP, standing alone in the electoral fight to elect [+ nsdap_candidate +], has little chance of winning—at least according to our advisors. However, this does not mean the election is inconsequential. The extensive <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazi</span> propaganda campaign, orchestrated by the infamous Joseph Goebbels, could significantly shift public opinion. [? if nsdap_candidate == "Hitler": Furthermore, Adolf Hitler possesses a remarkable charismatic ability, and his strategy of flying across Germany to deliver speeches to hundreds of thousands of otherwise indifferent voters each day rivals even that of Hindenburg. ?]

WIP

@candidate_selection

